index 0000000..0758f39
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/v2/03B-C3-A-SYNC-LIFECYCLE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Step 3B-C3-A — Sync Lifecycle Coexistence
+
+During C3-A, V1 owns `sync_queue` catalog operations and V2 owns `outbox_operations` inventory operations. The V2 runner defaults to `legacyBridgeMode: 'disabled'`; bridging remains an explicit handoff tool for C3-B, preventing duplicate category/catalog submission.
+
+`syncManager` now accepts an explicit user ID and only processes legacy rows whose payload or existing local entity proves ownership. Ambiguous rows remain untouched. Product/category pulls replace only the active user's Dexie partition; account data is never globally cleared.
+
+`SyncContext` serializes one lifecycle cycle: wait for IndexedDB, run ownership-safe V1 sync, recover stale receipt-less V2 syncing rows, run V2 with bridging disabled, then perform bounded succeeded cleanup. Auth session and generation checks prevent stale V1/V2 responses from writing after logout or account switch. C3-B must hand catalog writes to V2, add image staging, then explicitly retire the competing V1 runtime.
